course: dictionary
lesson: 4194
title: Gooey and sticky words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Gooey» describes something soft, sticky and wet, like melted cheese or a warm brownie. You can often see it, feel it or taste it. Use the words around it to check: what is sticky, and does it stick to your fingers?
explain: The example says, «Shop slime is a gooey mix of glue-like chemicals and water that holds a shape for a moment but flows slowly, neither properly solid nor liquid.» The clues are glue-like, water, holds a shape and flows slowly. So gooey means sticky and soft, somewhere between solid and liquid. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it.
explain: Gooey can also be informal, meaning too sweet and soppy. A «gooey love song» is full of soppy feelings, not sticky stuff. Read the clues: love song tells you the meaning is about feelings, not texture. Always ask which meaning fits the sentence.
fact: Gooey is an adjective. Its forms are gooey, gooier and gooiest.
fact: Gooey means soft, sticky and wet, like «gooey chocolate cake».
fact: Informal gooey means too sweet and sentimental, as in «a gooey love song».
fact: Phrases include «gooey brownies», «gooey slime» and «go all gooey», which means to become soppy.
fact: The example says shop slime «flows slowly» and is «neither properly solid nor liquid», so it is a good example of gooey.
exercise: «Shop slime is a gooey mix of glue-like chemicals and water.» What does gooey mean here? | Hard and shiny like glass | *Soft, sticky and wet | Loud and fizzy | Dry and crunchy
exercise: Ella says a love song is gooey. What might she mean? | It is made of glue | *It is too sweet and soppy, full of sentimental feelings | Melted cheese is on the song | It is very fast and loud
exercise: The example says slime is «neither properly solid nor liquid». Which best describes slime? | Solid like a rock | *Something in between solid and liquid | A gas that floats in the air | Liquid like water
test: Which word means soft and sticky? | *Gooey | Crunchy | Quick | Bright
test: Why should you wash your hands after playing with slime? | Because gooey things are dry | Because slime is always hot | Because slime makes you sleepy | *Because you should never eat slime, and it is sticky
exam: Which sentence uses gooey in the informal sense? | «The gooey cheese melted on the toast.» | *«The gooey love song made Dad groan.» | «The gooey brownies were warm and soft.» | «The gooey mix was poured into the tin.»
